        "content": "{\"formal\": {\"statement\": \"open Metric Filter Topology Set Nat in\\n∀ (H : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 4)))\\n    (H_def : H = {P : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 4) | ∀ i : Fin 4, |P i| ≤ 1 / 2})\\n    (contains : ℝ → Prop)\\n    (contains_def : ∀ r, contains r ↔\\n      ∃ᵉ (A : AffineSubspace ℝ (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 4))) (C ∈ A),\\n        Module.finrank ℝ A.direction = 2 ∧\\n        sphere C r ∩ A ⊆ H), IsGreatest contains putnam_2008_b3_solution\", \"namespace\": \"\", \"supporting_declarations\": [{\"name\": \"putnam_2008_b3_solution\", \"namespace\": \"\", \"type\": \"open Metric Filter Topology Set Nat in\\nℝ\", \"value\": \"@(open Metric Filter Topology Set Nat in\\n@((Real.sqrt 2 / 2)))\", \"scopes\": [\"Metric\", \"Filter\", \"Topology\", \"Set\", \"Nat\"]}], \"rendered\": \"∀ (H : (Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 4)))),\\n  ((H = {P | (∀ (i : (Fin 4)), (|(P.ofLp i)| ≤ (1 / 2)))}) →\\n    (∀ (contains : (ℝ → Prop)),\\n      ((∀ (r : ℝ),\\n          ((contains r) ↔\\n            (∃ A, (∃ C ∈ A, (((Module.finrank ℝ ↥A.direction) = 2) ∧ (((Metric.sphere C r) ∩ ↑A) ⊆ H)))))) →\\n        (IsGreatest contains putnam_2008_b3_solution))))\"}, \"signature\": \"(H : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 4)))\\n    (H_def : H = {P : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 4) | ∀ i : Fin 4, |P i| ≤ 1 / 2})\\n    (contains : ℝ → Prop)\\n    (contains_def : ∀ r, contains r ↔\\n      ∃ᵉ (A : AffineSubspace ℝ (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 4))) (C ∈ A),\\n        Module.finrank ℝ A.direction = 2 ∧\\n        sphere C r ∩ A ⊆ H) :\\n    IsGreatest contains putnam_2008_b3_solution\", \"informal\": \"What is the largest possible radius of a circle contained in a $4$-dimensional hypercube of side length $1$?\", \"docstring\": \"/--\\nWhat is the largest possible radius of a circle contained in a $4$-dimensional hypercube of side length $1$?\\n-/\", \"prechecks\": {\"status\": \"completed\", \"hints\": [{\"kind\": \"finite_index_review\", \"status\": \"advisory\"}, {\"kind\": \"division_review\", \"status\": \"advisory\"}], \"vacuity\": \"unresolved\"}, \"advisory\": {\"paraphrase_status\": \"completed\", \"differences\": [], \"paraphrase\": \"For every subset H of Euclidean space ℝ⁴, where H consists of all points P such that the absolute value of each coordinate of P is at most 1/2, the operation 'contains' is defined as follows: For any real number r, 'contains r' holds if and only if there exists an affine subspace A of dimension 2 within ℝ⁴ and a point C in A such that the sphere of radius r centered at C intersects A and is entirely contained within H. Furthermore, this operation 'contains' is the greatest such operation that satisfies the given conditions.\", \"comparison_status\": \"truncated\"}}"
